 "result_text": "`bytes_sql_quote()` in `src/DocumentTemplate/DT_Var.py` now returns text on Python 3, so quoted bytes can be concatenated with the rest of the SQL query string. I haven't run the tests or tried it on a real template.\n\nThe change does what your patch does: after removing and doubling the dangerous characters, it decodes the result as UTF-8. I limited the decode to Python 3, because on Python 2 `str` is already the string type and decoding would turn it into `unicode`.\n\nOne thing to be aware of: the decode is strict, so bytes that aren't valid UTF-8 now raise `UnicodeDecodeError` instead of passing through. I kept this because it matches the patch in the issue. If you'd rather not raise, I can add `errors='replace'`.",
